{"type":"lesson","title":"XGBoost in 5 minutes"}
{"say":"Today: XGBoost. Many small trees, built one after another, each fixing the last one's mistakes.","gist":"XGBoost = small trees fixing mistakes","actions":[{"type":"write","id":"title","text":"XGBoost = many small trees, in a row","at":{"region":"title"},"size":"title"}]}
{"say":"Let's predict house prices. Here are three houses and what they really cost.","gist":"Example: three house prices","actions":[{"type":"table","id":"houses","rows":[["house","size","price"],["A","50 m²","150k"],["B","80 m²","240k"],["C","120 m²","330k"]],"at":{"region":"main"}}]}
{"say":"Tree one makes a rough first guess: about 200k for every house.","gist":"Tree 1 guesses 200k for all","actions":[{"type":"box","id":"tree1","text":"Tree 1","note":"guesses 200k","at":{"right_of":"houses"}},{"type":"arrow","from":"houses","to":"tree1","label":"learns"}]}
{"say":"Now look at the mistakes. A mistake is the real price minus the guess.","gist":"Mistake = price − guess","actions":[{"type":"write","id":"mistake","text":"mistake = price − guess","at":{"region":"main"}},{"type":"mark","target":"mistake.mistake","style":"underline","note":"also called residual"}]}
{"say":"House A is 50k too high, B is 40k too low, and C is 130k too low. C is the worst.","gist":"Mistakes: A −50k, B +40k, C +130k","actions":[{"type":"bars","id":"miss","bars":[{"label":"A","value":-50},{"label":"B","value":40},{"label":"C","value":130}],"unit":"k","at":{"right_of":"mistake"}},{"type":"mark","target":"miss.C","style":"circle","note":"worst"}]}
{"say":"A common slip: thinking tree two learns the prices again. It does not.","gist":"Tree 2 does not relearn prices","actions":[{"type":"write","id":"wrong","text":"tree 2 learns the prices","at":{"region":"main"}},{"type":"strike","target":"wrong"}]}
{"say":"Tree two learns only the mistakes, and adds a small fix to the guess.","gist":"Tree 2 learns only the mistakes","actions":[{"type":"box","id":"tree2","text":"Tree 2","note":"learns the mistakes","at":{"right_of":"miss"}},{"type":"arrow","from":"miss","to":"tree2","label":"learns"}]}
{"say":"The final answer adds up every tree. The learning rate, eta, keeps each fix small.","gist":"Answer = sum of trees, scaled by η","actions":[{"type":"write","id":"sum","text":"ŷ = f₁(x) + η·f₂(x) + η·f₃(x) + …","at":{"region":"main"}},{"type":"mark","target":"sum.η","style":"circle","note":"learning rate"}]}
{"say":"House C's mistake shrinks with every tree: from 130k down to 12k after three trees.","gist":"Mistakes shrink with every tree","actions":[{"type":"bars","id":"shrink","bars":[{"label":"tree 1","value":130},{"label":"tree 2","value":45},{"label":"tree 3","value":12}],"unit":"k","at":{"right_of":"sum"}},{"type":"highlight","target":"shrink.tree 3"}]}
{"say":"Let's sum up.","gist":"Key points","actions":[{"type":"list","id":"keys","title":"Key points","items":["Trees are added one by one","Each tree learns the last mistakes","η keeps each fix small"],"at":{"region":"main"}}]}
{"say":"One more: stop adding trees when the mistakes stop shrinking.","gist":"Stop when mistakes stop shrinking","actions":[{"type":"list","id":"keys","items":["Stop when mistakes stop shrinking"],"at":{"region":"main"}}]}
